  "findings": "The adopted 2026–2027 regulations and Study Guide establish three 60 EC years in the English track. Year one includes literary analysis, theory, language, creative writing and adaptation. The diagnostic test and academic orientation carry no additional credits. The binding study advice requires at least 42 EC and both first-year Academic Skills courses. Year two includes one 3 EC language option, Pronunciation or Presentation. Year three includes 30 EC of approved open study, one two-course specialisation (12 EC), Career Orientation (6 EC), and an individual thesis including its colloquium (12 EC). Changing World 1 requires passing Literary Theory; Changing World 2 requires participation in the first course. Spring thesis entry requires passing all first- and second-year courses. The regulations specify a separate autumn entry rule. The English and Dutch tracks have separate curricula.",
  "authority": "Adopted 2026–2027 OER, English annual grid and final progression annex, plus exact current modules. Use one of the alternative language courses and one specialisation pair. English thesis is 12 EC with its colloquium; the separately listed Dutch colloquium is not added. Course L_ELBALES206 is Transatlantic Travel Writing and L_ALBALES206 is Cultural History. Source page 20 and current guide agree on the ledger; the chosen Changing World pair addresses a stable English direction independently of UCR."
}
